<ns0:section xmlns:ns0="http://xml.house.gov/schemas/uslm/1.0" style="-uslm-lc:I80" id="id4cfdb596-5dcd-11f1-b11b-9e551e93f87d" identifier="/us/usc/t34/s12252"><ns0:num value="12252">§ 12252.</ns0:num><ns0:heading> Eligibility to receive grants</ns0:heading><ns0:content>
<ns0:p style="-uslm-lc:I11" class="indent0">To be eligible to receive a grant under <ns0:ref href="/us/usc/t34/s12251">section 12251 of this title</ns0:ref>, a State shall submit to the Attorney General an application at such time, in such form, and containing such information as the Attorney General reasonably may require by rule.</ns0:p>
</ns0:content><ns0:sourceCredit id="id4cfdb597-5dcd-11f1-b11b-9e551e93f87d">(<ns0:ref href="/us/pl/103/322/tIII/s31912">Pub. L. 103–322, title III, § 31912</ns0:ref>, <ns0:date date="1994-09-13">Sept. 13, 1994</ns0:date>, <ns0:ref href="/us/stat/108/1895">108 Stat. 1895</ns0:ref>.)</ns0:sourceCredit>
<ns0:notes type="uscNote" id="id4cfdb598-5dcd-11f1-b11b-9e551e93f87d">
<ns0:note style="-uslm-lc:I74" role="crossHeading" topic="editorialNotes" id="id4cfdb599-5dcd-11f1-b11b-9e551e93f87d"><ns0:heading class="centered"><ns0:b>Editorial Notes</ns0:b></ns0:heading></ns0:note>
<ns0:note style="-uslm-lc:I76" topic="codification" id="id4cfdb59a-5dcd-11f1-b11b-9e551e93f87d"><ns0:heading class="centered smallCaps">Codification</ns0:heading>
<ns0:p style="-uslm-lc:I21" class="indent0">Section was formerly classified to <ns0:ref href="/us/usc/t42/s13892">section 13892 of Title 42</ns0:ref>, The Public Health and Welfare, prior to editorial reclassification and renumbering as this section.</ns0:p>
</ns0:note>
</ns0:notes>
</ns0:section>
